statement:
Let P, k ∈ ℕ and let g = (g_1, …, g_k) (g : Fin k → Euclid P) be an orthonormal family in ℝ^P with span G := span{g_1, …, g_k}; H^k := μHE[k]. Let ι : (Fin k → ℝ) → ℝ^P, ι(u) := Σ_i u_i·g_i, where Fin k → ℝ carries its product Lebesgue measure volume. Then:
(i) the push-forward of volume under ι is H^k restricted to G: (volume).map ι = H^k⌞G;
(ii) for every r > 0 the closed box {t ∈ G : |⟨g_i, t⟩| ≤ r for all i} and the open box {t ∈ G : |⟨g_i, t⟩| < r for all i} both have H^k-measure ENNReal.ofReal((2r)^k).
